{"name":"Espresso Tonic","hex":"#c18b5b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"espresso","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A concentrated coffee beverage brewed by forcing hot water under high pressure through finely ground coffee.","A drink that includes espresso as an ingredient."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/espresso"},{"term":"tonic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to tension, especially of the muscles.","Restorative; curative; or invigorating."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A substance with medicinal properties intended to restore or invigorate.","Tonic water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tonic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Espresso and tonic","blocks":[{"text":"Espresso and tonic or espresso tonic is a non-alcoholic mixed drink made by mixing espresso and tonic water. First recorded in 2007, the drink became popular in Scandinavia before spreading to North America, Japan, and around the world. The key ingredients are espresso and tonic water, but other flavourings may be added."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Espresso_and_tonic%2C_COFFEE_CITEN%2C_Akiha%2C_Niigata%2C_Niigata%2C_Japan%2C_May_2023.jpg/330px-Espresso_and_tonic%2C_COFFEE_CITEN%2C_Akiha%2C_Niigata%2C_Niigata%2C_Japan%2C_May_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Espresso_and_tonic"},{"title":"Espresso","blocks":[{"text":"Espresso is a concentrated form of coffee produced by forcing hot water under high pressure through finely ground coffee beans. Originating in Italy, espresso has become one of the most popular coffee-brewing methods worldwide. It is characterized by its small serving size, typically 25–30 ml, and its distinctive layers: a dark body topped with a lighter-colored foam called \"crema\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Tazzina_di_caff%C3%A8_a_Ventimiglia.jpg/330px-Tazzina_di_caff%C3%A8_a_Ventimiglia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Espresso"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Espresso_tonic.jpg/500px-Espresso_tonic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Espresso_tonic.jpg/1280px-Espresso_tonic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Espresso_tonic.jpg/500px-Espresso_tonic.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Espresso tonic, with head (Montevideo, 2023)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEspresso_tonic.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg/500px-Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg/1280px-Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg/500px-Victoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A man pulls an espresso while leaning out of a train in a 1922 advertisement for a \"caffé espresso\" machine. The imagery references the shared associations of speed and steam, as well as name: in Italy, a class of trains is called \"espresso\".[11]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVictoria_Arduino%2C_1922.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/Angelo-moriondo-portrait-espresso-machine-inventor.jpg/330px-Angelo-moriondo-portrait-espresso-machine-inventor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.or